.TH UDS 1 "2026-07-25" "Universal Device SDK" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uds \- Universal Device SDK command-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uds
[\fI--config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fI--log-level\fR \fIlevel\fR] [\fI--output\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fI--transport\fR \fIname\fR] [\fI--device\fR \fIid\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Universal Device SDK (UDS) is a cross-platform, CLI-first developer platform for
embedded device development across heterogeneous hardware architectures.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize a new UDS project directory.
.TP
.B devices
List and discover connected devices. Use \fB--scan\fR for active discovery.
.TP
.B inspect
Show detailed information about a connected device.
.TP
.B doctor
Run system diagnostics: check transports, configuration, and connectivity.
.TP
.B logs
Tail device logs with optional level filtering.
.TP
.B monitor
Real-time device monitoring with console output.
.TP
.B flash
Flash a firmware image to a connected device.
.TP
.B update
OTA firmware update with rollback support.
.TP
.B benchmark
Run latency and throughput benchmarks.
.TP
.B plugins
Manage UDS plugins (list, install, remove).
.TP
.B rpc
Invoke an RPC method manually.
.TP
.B fs
Filesystem operations on device (ls, cat, cp, mv, rm, mkdir).
.TP
.B build
Build firmware from source for a target device.
.TP
.B firmware
Manage firmware images (list, verify, sign).
.TP
.B generate
Generate code from UDS IDL definitions.
.TP
.B docs
Open documentation.
.TP
.B version
Print version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIfile\fR
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.uds/config.toml).
.TP
.B \-\-log-level \fIlevel\fR
Set log level: error, warn, info, debug, trace (default: info).
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human).
.TP
.B \-\-transport \fIname\fR
Transport to use: serial, tcp, udp, ws, ble, usb, mock.
.TP
.B \-\-device \fIid\fR
Target device ID.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
0
Success
.TP
1
General error
.TP
2
Usage error
.TP
3
Device error
.TP
4
Network error
.TP
5
Configuration error
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.uds/config.toml
User configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at https://github.com/dupewon/Universal-Device-SDK/docs
